{
  "capture": "telemetry/dev-v006-2A-D/opamp-temperature/capture-1",
  "notes": "DC laps on the bare load at four plateaus of a printer bed, the load on the bed too, meter route ammeter on the 20 A range at room in capture-1, and the same laps a day later in telemetry/dev-v006-2A-D/opamp-temperature/capture-2 on route rs1, the meter on the 220 mV range across the Rs1 pads, with a rest stream of the chip's 1.2 V reference at a 5.5 V rail before each plateau's laps; one line per plateau through counts over the lap's own zero against the meter's amps; gain_drift_pct_per_c is the line through the four plateaus' gain_pct against the board NTC through ntc-curve's beta_nominal, its design conversion, with its standard error as the bounds, gain_drift_pooled_pct_per_c the one-offset model over all forty rows; a plateau's board_c is the mean over its laps' drives with the spread over the laps as lo/hi, and beyond that it carries ntc-curve's grade, the meter's class of 1 % + 0.5 C and the bed gradient, 1.1 C at the hot plateau; gain_drift_max_pct is the hot plateau against room; reversibility_pct is room-again against room with both errors; ntc_move_in_lap_c is the NTC's fall through the 7.6 V lap at the room plateaus, ntc_move_over_laps_c the fall from the first lap's rest to the last's there; amp_drift_pct_per_c and amp_drift_pooled_pct_per_c are the same two estimators on capture-2's counts per millivolt of shunt, the amplifier and the ADC with the shunt out of the route, amp_drift_max_pct its hot plateau against room; vdd_v per plateau in plateaus_rs1 is the rest stream's mean with the stream's spread as lo/hi, read to about a count of vref_raw, and vdd_drift_pct_per_c the line through the four; shunt_drift_pct_per_c is gain_drift_pct_per_c less amp_drift_pct_per_c with the errors in quadrature, the shunt's own resistance change, shunt_drift_max_pct the same at the hot plateau, against the part's rating of 50 ppm per C either way; the *_hot_ratio_pct_per_c keys are the per-lap ratio at the hot plateau over each capture's own room to hot span, the estimator that resolves the split; the two captures are a day apart on the same board and rig",
